{"ts": 1791256068.6153128, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Quick correction on the eval idea: **pass^k** means *all* k runs succeed, not \u201csome of them.\u201d\n\nTry this memory hook: \n- **pass@k** = at least one of k works\n- **pass^k** = every one of k works\n\nThis matters because Friday\u2019s build is about reliability. If your environment definition is good but only works sometimes, pass^k will catch that.\n\nCan you reply with one sentence explaining why pass^k is the right metric for this build?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=10 messages 2m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 10, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.4803775885073101}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8218151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
