{"ts": 1791256076.352314, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "No worries \u2014 here\u2019s the simple version:\n\n- **pass@k** = at least **one** of the k tries works\n- **pass^k** = **every single one** of the k tries works\n\nSo if you run the build on 3 seeds:\n- 3/3 successes = pass^3\n- 2/3 successes = not pass^3\n- 1/3 successes = not pass^3\n\nFor Friday\u2019s build, you want **pass^k** because the point is reliability: it should work consistently, not just sometimes.\n\nIf it helps, think of it like this: **pass@k asks \u201cCan it work?\u201d** and **pass^k asks \u201cDoes it always work?\u201d**", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=14 idle 4m", "t": 18, "activity": [{"t": 14, "app": "idle", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.4803775885073101}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8378151230937745, "motivation": 0.494715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 4, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
